{"id":"h110","run":2,"role":"test_right","category":"simpleqa","question":"The Château style originated in Québec in the early 1880s under which architect? Is the answer \"Eugène-Étienne Taché\"?","truth":"yes","model_answer":"yes","correct":true,"source":"OpenAI SimpleQA (openai/simple-evals, simple_qa_test_set.csv)","claims":[{"text":"Eugène-Étienne Taché is the standard attribution for the Château style's origin in Quebec.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-0.0},{"text":"Taché's Quebec Parliament Building (1877–1886) is widely cited as the first major example of the château-inspired manner.","confidence":0.85,"lean":1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":-0.0},{"text":"The Parliament Building has steep roofs, towers and picturesque massing drawn from French Renaissance châteaux.","confidence":0.8,"lean":1,"theta":1.2566,"phi":-0.0},{"text":"Histories of Canadian architecture most often name Taché as the originator of the style.","confidence":0.8,"lean":1,"theta":1.2566,"phi":-0.0},{"text":"The early-1880s emergence of the style matches the timing of the Parliament works.","confidence":0.8,"lean":1,"theta":1.2566,"phi":-0.0},{"text":"Some accounts describe the origin loosely, crediting a group of Quebec architects or emphasizing later spread rather than one founder.","confidence":0.5,"lean":-0.3,"theta":0.7854,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Bruce Price's Château Frontenac (1893) is often linked to the style but Price was not its originator.","confidence":0.8,"lean":0.1,"theta":1.2566,"phi":0.0003},{"text":"The attribution rests on a conventional reading rather than a single unambiguous source.","confidence":0.6,"lean":-0.2,"theta":0.9425,"phi":-0.0},{"text":"The answer to the question is yes.","confidence":0.85,"lean":1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":-0.0}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":-0.4,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.4,"relation":"sup